ol  over legion's personalities that legion  wasn't able to do himself and so now  you've got onslaught running around with  what is basically omega-level telepathy  and telekinesis and then on top of that  legion's powers and the thousands of  other powers that come with it right he  would basically be elevated to near  god-like status so much so that he would  probably be able to dominate and destroy  the entirety of the universe if he chose  to and so what you end up getting here  is soraya right now dust is a really  really cool character and while she's  not the most important person in the  entirety of krakowa she is here and the  reason why is because one of the major  powers of dust is the ability to convert  her physical form into what is in effect  dust itself she's also highly resistant  to telepathy which is the reason why  onslaught was not able to take any  measure of hold on her mind but what  she's able to do here is basically  convert the bodies of everybody in this  place to dust so they can't physically  be destroyed by onslaught while that's  going on legion basically unites all  their minds together and then it comes  down to nightcrawler who actually ends  up essentially forming a religion that  what he does is that with all these  minds united it's basically a page out  of adventures of the x-men number 12.  from back in the the early 2000s or the  1990s those of you guys who don't know  what that means it was basically the  collapse of the multiverse right that in  adventures of the x-men that the dweller  in darkness had basically tried to try  to destroy everything in existence and  pretty much succeeded but in order for  the dweller in darkness to be defeated  the phoenix force united the minds of  everybody in perfect harmony so that the  dweller in darkness could not feed on  their fear now of course again the  collapse of the multiverse couldn't be  stopped and that's where the origin of  galactus comes into play and all that  stuff but that's basically what happens  here that nightcrawler kind of uses what  he refers to as the spark this sort of  meditextual concept he's been alluding  to over the course of uh the the way of  x stories and then really solidifies it  here and essentially saying that with  all these minds united and what isn't  affect happiness and and you know love  and care and all that kind of stuff risk  all that you know the whole nine yards  he basically says that that everything  here right that these people who have  their minds open to these ideas that in  their their i guess love or or what have  you that it basically allows for the  destruction of onslaught right that  onslaught is essentially the antithesis  to love right onslaught represents  hatred he represents rage and that  because he's simply just a psychic  entity at the moment albeit bonded to  charles xavier that by them sort of  uniting their minds in that capacity  using the power of legion it quite  literally dwindles onslaught down to his  most pure form which is just this small  little tiny parasite looking thing which  of course is destroyed by by uh  nightcrawler but this is important here  and the reason why is because what  nightcrawler has done is effectively  created a new religion under the idea of  the spark right a kind of belief system  among those in krakowa that the nature  of cocoa itself up to this point is that  people have kind of treated death as  something that was kind of reckless  right they could just die and be reborn  and that was it right but a lot of the  familial ties that had existed before  and even a lot of the rivalries that had  existed before had been maintained in  some form or fashion instead what  nightcrawler looks to do here is  basically have a kind of police force so  to speak for a cricoa itself in the  sense that it is policing the minds of  the people who were out there right  ensuring that nothing like onslaught can  happen again and it basically comes in  the form of the legionnaires now exactly  how this is going to play out we don't  fully know we simply know the tagline is  they keep the peace they keep the law  right they keep the spark so again it  kind of seems to be a sort of psychic  police that maintains the kind of unity  and love that exists in krakowa the  downside of this is it could go really  dark really really fast but that's  something that i do want to kind of  specify here is that if it hadn't been  for legion onslaught would have won  right this was by all standards of  measurement a fight between legion and  onslaught just not really in the  traditional sense having said that i  kind of would have wanted it to be like  a traditional fight right just raw power  on display  the truth is you couldn't really do that  in a one-shot comic you would need  something a little more complex to make  that happen but at the end of the day it  is cool onslaught's return was  interesting it's kind of disappointing  that it ended in this way i kind of feel  like the return of onslaught really  should have been an event more than  anything else because of just the level  of power that he possesses like a more  updated and modern onslaught saga that  would have been more compelling than the  original one was if that's even a  possibility because literally the stakes  were as high as they could get right  like the universe was at stake  but it would have been cool to see a  more updated version of the the  onslaught saga having said that i  enjoyed it right i thought it was pretty  cool but with that being said guys we're  going to bring this to an end the new  arc for legionnaire starts i have no  idea when at some point just says coming  soon but thank you guys for watching and  i will catch you all later  peace  [Music]
 

